# PM2.5 and O3 monitor propensity-score balancing scripts

This repository contains R scripts for ZCTA-level propensity-score balancing for PM2.5 and O3 monitor locations.

There are two analysis scripts:

- `R/01_make_ps_balance_pm25.R`: PM2.5 monitor workflow using `MS.INFO.shp`
- `R/02_make_ps_balance_o3.R`: O3 monitor workflow using `MS.O3.INFO.shp`

The scripts pull ZCTA-level demographic/socioeconomic variables from the Census API, build an adjusted ZCTA shapefile, intersect monitor locations with ZCTAs, fit propensity-score models, create PS groups, and export final CSV/RData files.

## What users need to do

Users only need to edit one file:

```text
R/00_config.R
```

Open `R/00_config.R` and replace the placeholder values with the paths on your computer.

```r
CENSUS_API_KEY <- "PASTE_YOUR_CENSUS_API_KEY_HERE"

ZCTA_RAW_SHP <- "/path/to/cb_2020_us_zcta520_500k.shp"
BG_SHP <- "/path/to/cb_2023_17_bg_500k.shp"
UA_BLOCK_CSV <- "/path/to/2020_UA_BLOCK_IL.csv"

PM25_MONITOR_SHP <- "/path/to/MS.INFO.shp"
O3_MONITOR_SHP <- "/path/to/MS.O3.INFO.shp"

OUT_DIR <- "data/outputs/PSBalancing"
```

Do not upload your real Census API key to GitHub.

## Required input files

| Config variable | File needed | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `ZCTA_RAW_SHP` | `cb_2020_us_zcta520_500k.shp` | 2020 ZCTA cartographic boundary shapefile. Keep `.shp`, `.shx`, `.dbf`, `.prj` together. |
| `BG_SHP` | `cb_2023_17_bg_500k.shp` | 2023 Illinois block-group shapefile. Keep `.shp`, `.shx`, `.dbf`, `.prj` together. |
| `UA_BLOCK_CSV` | `2020_UA_BLOCK_IL.csv` | Illinois urban-area block CSV with at least `STATE`, `COUNTY`, `TRACT`, `BLOCK`. |
| `PM25_MONITOR_SHP` | `MS.INFO.shp` | PM2.5 monitor point shapefile. Keep `.shp`, `.shx`, `.dbf`, `.prj` together. |
| `O3_MONITOR_SHP` | `MS.O3.INFO.shp` | O3 monitor point shapefile. Keep `.shp`, `.shx`, `.dbf`, `.prj` together. |

## Install R packages

From the repository root:

```bash
Rscript R/00_install_packages.R
```

Required R packages:

- `tidycensus`
- `dplyr`
- `sf`
- `stringr`
- `mgcv`
- `data.table`

## Check input files

After editing `R/00_config.R`, run:

```bash
Rscript R/00_check_inputs.R
```

This checks that the files listed in `R/00_config.R` exist. For shapefiles, `.shp`, `.shx`, and `.dbf` must be in the same folder. `.prj` is strongly recommended.

## Run everything

Run both PM2.5 and O3 workflows:

```bash
Rscript R/99_run_all.R
```

Or run them separately:

```bash
Rscript R/01_make_ps_balance_pm25.R
Rscript R/02_make_ps_balance_o3.R
```

## Final outputs

By default, outputs are written to:

```text
data/outputs/PSBalancing/
```

Expected final files:

```text
PSB_PM25_new.csv
MS_INFO_PS_PM25_new.RData
PSB_Ozone_new.csv
MS_INFO_PS_Ozone_new.RData
```

The PM2.5 script also creates an adjusted ZCTA shapefile:

```text
data/outputs/PSBalancing/zcta_adjusted/cb_2020_us_zcta520_500k_Adjusted.shp
```

The O3 script reuses this adjusted ZCTA file if it exists; otherwise, it rebuilds it from the raw ZCTA/BG/UA paths in `R/00_config.R`.

## Notes for GitHub sharing

Do not commit:

- your real Census API key
- private monitor shapefiles, unless sharing is allowed
- generated `.csv`, `.RData`, or shapefile outputs

If monitor shapefiles cannot be shared, include a synthetic example monitor shapefile with the same columns and point geometry.
